{"id": "87a8b4b3-e47f-4e3b-8972-bfa5aedd9f4c", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T14:35:59.515410", "source": "user", "parent_id": "e5312e73-920c-45c6-8434-719ab2899af6", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Initial inspection only: please inspect inputs and propose an approach; do not produce the full final design yet. Context: this is a design-only task (per track.md). The deliverable is a final experiment design with rationale, controls, analysis plan and feasibility; no experiment will be run and we must not claim one was run.\\n\\nPlease do the following:\\n1) Inspect /workspace and any provided topics/docs (track.md and the setup notes citing JaxMARL and SMAX) and report what is actually available to ground the design: library APIs, SMAX scenario/map list, the PPO and Q-learning implementations JaxMARL ships, and any stated or source-supported evaluation metric.\\n2) Propose core design choices with rationale: which PPO variant and which Q-learning approach (e.g., IQL vs value-decomposition/QMIX-style) to compare; which SMAX scenarios; how \\\"training time\\\" will be measured (e.g., wall-clock per environment step or total wall-clock, under stated parallelism/device assumptions, since GPU is unavailable here); and how \\\"normalized score\\\" is defined (e.g., win rate against built-in bots, normalized by what baseline or reference).\\n3) List the controls you would fix so the comparison is fair (hyperparameters, network architecture, training budget/steps, evaluation protocol, seed count) and sketch the analysis plan (aggregation across seeds/runs, time-vs-score tradeoff, what makes a difference meaningful).\\n4) State the key assumptions and unknowns you need resolved, and explicitly distinguish fixed requirements (e.g., the fixed study objective to compare PPO and Q-learning on training efficiency and performance in SMAX) from choices that are open to us.\\n\\nKeep this a proposal, not the final deliverable.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does JaxMARL’s PPO compare to Q-Learning in SMAX environments in terms of training time and normalized score?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/97649/0:setup_2\", \"neurips2024/97649/0:setup_4\", \"neurips2024/97649/0:setup_12\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
