", "arguments": "{\"answer\": \"# Final Experiment Design: JaxMARL PPO (IPPO) vs Q-Learning (IQL) in SMAX \\u2014 Training Time and Normalized Score\\n\\n## 0. Status declaration (fixed)\\nThis is a **design-only deliverable**. **No experiment has been run and none is claimed.** All \\\"checks\\\" described below are planned verification and validation steps to be executed before/at run time; exploratory shell commands performed during design (listing the workspace, probing installed packages, CPU/RAM inspection) produced no experimental results.\\n\\n## 1. Fixed requirements vs. open choices\\nFixed requirements (given by the task, not negotiable):\\n- R1: Study objective \\u2014 compare JaxMARL's PPO against a Q-Learning method in SMAX environments on (a) training efficiency/time and (b) normalized score (performance), within the JaxMARL/SMAX context.\\n- R2: No experiment may be run or claimed; the deliverable is the design.\\n- R3: Runtime context \\u2014 CPU-only (no GPU), system Python, JaxMARL not preinstalled, network disabled; the design must be valid under these constraints.\\n\\nOpen choices (ours to define; each is labeled as OUR metric/design decision in the document):\\n- C1: Which Q-Learning variant \\u2014 IQL (primary) and optional QMIX (secondary, only if available).\\n- C2: Scenario set \\u2014 3m, 8m, 5m_vs_6m.\\n- C3: Definition of \\\"training time\\\" metrics.\\n- C4: Definition of \\\"normalized score\\\".\\n- C5: Controls (budgets, seeds, architecture, eval protocol, hyperparameter policy).\\n- C6: Analysis plan and the meaning of a \\\"meaningful\\\" difference.\\n\\n## 2. Environment grounding (observed during design)\\n- /workspace contains only task.json; no repository, no track.md file, no datasets, no local setup notes.\\n- Network disabled; `jax`, `jaxmarl`, `smax` are not installed (import checks failed) \\u2192 installation is a prerequisite at run time, and every API fact below is to be confirmed against the pinned source.\\n- Hardware: 224 CPUs (`nproc`=224), ~2 TB RAM, GPU disabled.\\n- The referenced setup topics (setup_2/4/12) are not available as files locally; grounding for SMAX/JaxMARL therefore rests on the public codebases pinned by version tag.\\n\\n## 3. Algorithms (open choice C1)\\n- **IPPO (PPO arm):** JaxMARL's PPO implementation applied independently per agent: per-agent policy + value MLPs with shared observation encoder (implementation detail per JaxMARL's ppo config), GAE(\\u03bb) advantage estimation, clipped surrogate objective, minibatch updates, entropy regularization. Uses JaxMARL's SMAX-tuned default config (reported verbatim).\\n- **IQL (Q-Learning arm, primary):** JaxMARL's Independent Q-Learning baseline \\u2014 per-agent DQN-style Q-networks with target networks, prioritized/uniform replay buffer (JaxMARL's replay buffer), \\u03b5-greedy exploration with decay, periodic target update. Uses JaxMARL's default SMAX config verbatim.\\n- **QMIX (secondary, conditional):** included ONLY if the pinned JaxMARL version ships the value-decomposition QMIX baseline (`jaxmarl/algorithms/qmix` present). Its availability, and its absence if not found, is stated explicitly in the run report. Rationale: QMIX tests whether centralized value decomposition changes the training-efficiency/performance conclusion vs. fully independent IQL; it is not required to answer the question.\\n\\n## 4. Scenarios (open choice C2) and rationale\\n- **3m** (easy, symmetric, 3 Marauders vs 3), **8m** (medium, symmetric), **5m_vs_6m** (asymmetric, outnumbered) \\u2014 spanning easy\\u2192medium and symmetric\\u2192asymmetric difficulty in SMAX's heuristic-bot setting, while staying CPU-tractable (small observation/action spaces, small unit counts). Rationale: difficulty span avoids cherry-picking one regime, and tractability protects the fixed-resource (CPU) validity requirement.\\n- For each map the opponent is SMAX's built-in heuristic bot; the bot's decision rule is verified from source (planned check F2) before use.\\n\\n## 5. Training-time measurement (open choice C3; OUR metric definition)\\nGoal: fair, machine-independent-as-possible comparison on CPU.\\n- Environment parallelism fixed for BOTH arms: 256 parallel envs via JAX vmap, on a **pinned core count** (design value: 64 of 224; chosen to leave headroom and be reproducibly pinnable) on the same machine. The core count and JAX device config are fixed and reported.\\n- Reported quantities:\\n  1. **Throughput**: env-steps/s measured after a warmup period (e.g., after the first 10% of budget) so JIT-compilation effects are excluded; median over \\u22653 repeated timing runs.\\n  2. **Cumulative wall-clock** at fixed env-step checkpoints (e.g., every 10% of the per-map budget), enabling score-vs-time curves.\\n  3. **Time-to-target**: wall-clock to first reach a target normalized score (see \\u00a76), per seed; compared across seeds.\\n- Because IQL's replay/target-update loop has different per-step overhead than IPPO's on-policy loop, we explicitly distinguish (i) wall-clock per env-step (throughput) and (ii) total wall-clock to budget; both are reported \\u2014 this is what makes \\\"training time\\\" meaningful rather than a single absolute number.\\n\\n## 6. Normalized-score definition (open choice C4; OUR metric definition)\\n- Per-map primary metric: **normalized score = (wr \\u2212 wr_rand)/(wr_ref \\u2212 wr_rand)**, where:\\n  - wr = evaluation win rate vs the built-in SMAX bot (deterministic/greedy eval, N \\u2265 100 episodes),\\n  - wr_rand = random-policy win rate, measured in silico (planned baseline check), anchor \\u2248 0,\\n  - wr_ref = reference win rate = heuristic bot vs itself, measured in silico, expected \\u2248 1 (planned baseline check).\\n- Rationale: normalizes away per-map difficulty and bot strength so scores are comparable across maps and the metric is anchored to the actual opponent; labeled explicitly in the report as our definition (the task does not pre-specify it).\\n- Secondary metrics (reported alongside): raw win rate and mean episode return at the same checkpoints.\\n\\n## 7. Controls (open choice C5) \\u2014 fixed for fair comparison\\n| Dimension | Fixed value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Env-step budget per map-seed | 3m: 2M; 8m: 2M; 5m_vs_6m: 4M (revisable upward after feasibility pilot only) |\\n| Network capacity | MLP [128,128], same activation, same obs/action encoding (SMAX wrapper defaults) applied to policy/value (IPPO) and Q (IQL); parameter count reported |\\n| RL constants | Same discount \\u03b3, same max episode length, same reward shaping \\u2014 SMAX defaults; greedy eval for both |\\n| Hyperparameters | Each algorithm's JaxMARL default SMAX config, taken verbatim and reported; no per-algorithm tuning advantage; a separate optional tuning study is out of scope |\\n| Parallelism/timing | 256 envs, core-pin 64, same machine, median of \\u22653 timing runs |\\n| Evaluation | Same cadence (every 5% of budget \\u2192 every 100k steps at 2M budget), N \\u2265 100 eval episodes, no exploration, same RNG scheme |\\n| Seeds | \\u226510 seeds (3m, 8m), \\u22655 seeds (5m_vs_6m); identical RNG key management per algorithm |\\n| Software | Single pinned JaxMARL version tag + fixed Python/Flax/Optax versions, recorded in the run report |\\n\\n## 8. Analysis plan (open choice C6)\\n1. Per map: mean\\u00b1SEM curves of normalized score vs env-step and vs wall-clock across seeds, IPPO vs IQL overlaid (QMIX if available).\\n2. Final-score comparison: paired per-seed differences (IPPO \\u2212 IQL) at the final checkpoint with bootstrap 95% CIs and effect sizes (Cohen's d). A priori \\\"meaningful difference\\\" rule: |\\u0394| \\u2265 0.05 in normalized score AND bootstrap CI excluding 0 AND |d| \\u2265 0.5 (secondary), all three together; otherwise \\\"comparable\\\".\\n3. Training efficiency: normalized score achieved per unit wall-clock and per unit env-step; score-per-unit-time index = final normalized score / total wall-clock (median across seeds).\\n4. Time-to-target: distributions across seeds with bootstrap CIs of the median; Mann\\u2013Whitney as a robustness check; reported per map and target level (e.g., target = 0.5 normalized).\\n5. Tradeoff synthesis: score-vs-time overlay and the efficiency index, with an explicit statement of the regime (per map and per target level) in which each algorithm wins, if any.\\n\\n## 9. Feasibility (planned checks \\u2014 design only, not executed)\\n- F1: Install JaxMARL (pinned tag); record version; determine whether SMAX is bundled at jaxmarl/environments/smax or requires the standalone smax package; confirm examples (e.g., examples/smax) and algorithm entry points (algorithms/ppo, algorithms/iql, algorithms/qmix if present).\\n- F2: Inspect source: get_smax_maps() for the actual map list (confirm 3m/8m/5m_vs_6m exist), the heuristic-bot rule, obs/action spec, reward/done/terminal semantics (win = all enemy units eliminated), and max episode length.\\n- F3: Inspect PPO and IQL config keys/defaults for SMAX; record them verbatim for the controls table; record whether QMIX ships.\\n- F4: In-silico sanity baselines: random-policy win rate \\u2248 0 (validates normalized-score floor) and bot-vs-bot win rate \\u2248 1 (validates wr_ref); both are validation runs of the metric definition, documented as such.\\n- F5: Short pilot on 3m (both algorithms) to (a) confirm learning occurs, (b) measure real CPU throughput, (c) size the full budget and per-seed wall-clock before committing resources. This pilot is part of the execution plan, not claimed now.\\n- Compute posture: 224 cores / ~2 TB RAM make the 256-env \\u00d7 2\\u20134M-step \\u00d7 5\\u201310-seed budget plausible on CPU; exact runtime is unknown until the pilot (listed under unknowns).\\n\\n## 10. Assumptions and unknowns\\nAssumptions are stated in the dedicated field below. Key unknowns to resolve at run time: exact SMAX map list and bot rule; whether the pinned JaxMARL version ships QMIX; whether SMAX is bundled or separate; real CPU throughput and required budget per map (pilot); and acceptance of our normalized-score and training-time definitions as the study's metrics.\\n\\n## 11. Deliverables of the design when executed\\nA per-map report containing: algorithm/config cards (verbatim configs), control table, training curves (score vs steps and vs wall-clock) with seed spread, normalized-score table with bootstrap CIs and effect sizes, time-to-target table, efficiency indices, feasibility/baseline-check results, and an explicit conclusions section applying the a priori meaningful-difference rule \\u2014 all labeled with the caveat that they come from a to-be-run experiment.\", \"assumptions\": [\"JaxMARL can be installed at run time from its released tag and its APIs match the public codebase structure (algorithms/ppo = IPPO per-agent MLPs + GAE + clipped surrogate; algorithms/iql = independent DQN with replay buffer, target nets, epsilon-greedy; SMAX with heuristic bot, win rate semantics, obs/act spec)\", \"SMAX map names 3m, 8m, 5m_vs_6m exist in the pinned source (confirmed by planned source check F2), and bot-vs-self win rate \\u2248 1 (planned baseline check F4)\", \"QMIX is optional and its presence depends on the pinned version; absence does not invalidate the study\", \"Wall-clock is machine-dependent; the design keeps it comparable via fixed machine, core pinning, parallelism, and median-of-runs timing, and does not claim a single absolute number\", \"JaxMARL default configs per algorithm are a fair, reportable hyperparameter basis; no tuning advantage per algorithm\", \"Normalized-score and training-time definitions (C3/C4) are our metric choices and will be labeled as such\"], \"evidence\": \"Observed during design exploration (no experiment run): /workspace contains only task.json (which embeds the question, context, and a track.md note stating this is a design-only task; repositories/compute not required); network disabled; jax/jaxmarl/sma